    summary: 'A dog-boarding experience built on trust, visibility and consistency: verified kennels, structured pet profiles and real-time updates, so dog parents can confidently leave their dog in someone else’s care.',
    tags: ['Research', 'Information architecture', 'Prototyping', 'Conceptualising', 'Usability testing', 'Interviews'],
    problemTitle: 'Problem statement',
    problem: "Urban dog parents in India lack access to a reliable and verified boarding network. Most existing options are unregulated, with no standard protocols for care, hygiene or safety. The absence of real-time updates or proof of activity during a pet’s stay creates anxiety and distrust, especially for working professionals and frequent travellers who are unable to monitor their dog’s well-being from afar.",
